move-bringup (1.0.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ablspi-move-cm5.dts: rewrote against the actual CM5/RP1 topology
    after verifying the upstream raspberrypi/linux base DTBs
    (bcm2712-rpi-cm5-{cm4io,cm5io}.dtb). The previous overlay was a
    CM4-by-analogy stub that targeted &i2c0if / &i2c0mux / &i2c0_gpio44
    — labels that do not exist on CM5, where carrier-side GPIO/SPI/I²C
    live on the RP1 southbridge instead of the BCM2712 SoC. With those
    unresolved labels the Pi firmware would silently fail the whole
    overlay apply, taking ablspi down with it.
    The new overlay:
      - keeps &spi0 + irq-gpios=<&gpio 3 0>; both labels resolve to
        RP1 (spi@50000 / gpio@d0000), CS0 stays on physical SODIMM
        GPIO 8 per the base DTB's cs-gpios, ablspi-dkms binds via
        compatible="ablspi" unchanged.
      - targets &i2c5 (not &i2c0) for the PCF85063 RTC, because on
        CM5/RP1 the alt-function for the 44/45 pin pair is i2c5, not
        i2c0. The upstream pinctrl group `rp1_i2c5_44_45` (function=
        i2c5, pins=gpio44+gpio45, drive-strength=12mA, bias-pull-up)
        is drop-in correct — no manual mux.
      - drops the i2c0mux/i2c0if disable fragments entirely. They were
        a CM4 BCM2711 quirk; on CM5 those nodes are empty placeholders.
    Verified by compiling the .dtbo and confirming all four __fixups__
    labels (spi0, gpio, i2c5, rp1_i2c5_44_45) resolve against both
    cm4io and cm5io base DTBs.
  * config.txt: strip the family's `dtoverlay=dwc2,dr_mode=host` from
    the [cm5] block before appending our `dr_mode=otg` line. On CM5
    the BCM2712 USB controller at /axi/usb@480000 is dwc2-compatible
    ("brcm,bcm2835-usb", status=disabled), and the stock dwc2.dtbo
    applies cleanly via the &usb fixup — but the Armbian/RPi family
    default routes it host-only for [cm5], which would conflict with
    our Move/NCM-gadget OTG requirement. Mirrors the existing [cm4]
    `otg_mode=1` strip, done in both move-bringup.postinst and the
    Armbian board hook (move.csc pre_umount_final_image__zzz_move_finalise).

 -- Move Port <move-port@localhost>  Thu, 15 May 2026 21:00:00 +0000

move-bringup (1.0.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * move-web.service: three fixes that had it crash-looping since boot.
    - Group=ableton → Group=users. There is no `ableton` group (the
      ableton user's primary group is `users`, gid 100) so the unit
      died with status=216/GROUP before ExecStart fired — same trap
      already documented in move-launcher.service.
    - start-stop-daemon path corrected from /usr/bin to /usr/sbin
      (Debian ships it in /usr/sbin with a /sbin symlink); the wrong
      path failed ExecStart/ExecStop with status=203/EXEC.
    - Added AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE so MoveWebService,
      running as User=ableton, can bind privileged port 80 instead of
      dying with "HttpServer couldn't start listening".
  * mDNS / Bonjour: depend on avahi-daemon and libnss-mdns, and have
    the postinst enable+start avahi-daemon. The device now advertises
    itself as move.local with no DNS, and MoveLauncher's
    org.freedesktop.Avahi D-Bus hostname query stops erroring. postinst
    also ensures /etc/hostname and the 127.0.1.1 /etc/hosts entry are
    `move` on the dpkg -i-on-a-running-target path (customize-image.sh
    already pre-seeds this for image builds).

