move-bringup (1.0.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * /data and its subtree (CoreLibrary, Scratch, settings, UserData)
    are now root:users mode 2775 (setgid, group-writable) instead of
    root:root 0755. Stock AbletonOS has /data top-level as root:root
    0755 — ableton can only write under /data/UserData/ there. We
    loosen the top level so ableton (primary group `users`, gid 100)
    can drop files directly under /data/, which is needed for
    development, third-party userspace (vimana2r, schwung), and
    custom scripts the ableton user runs from its home. setgid
    ensures new files inherit group=users for symmetry. /data/log
    stays 1777 (sticky, world-writable) for shared log access.

 -- Move Port <move-port@localhost>  Wed, 13 May 2026 19:45:00 +0000

move-bringup (1.0.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * move-launcher.service:
    - Type=forking → Type=simple. MoveLauncher does NOT double-fork to
      daemonize; with forking systemd would TimeoutStartSec it out
      before it announced readiness and then SIGTERM the process.
    - Group=ableton → Group=users. The `ableton` user's primary group
      is `users` (gid 100) per the stock AbletonOS layout; there is no
      `ableton` group, and the old setting crashed the unit with
      status=216/GROUP before ExecStart could even fire.
    - SupplementaryGroups expanded to ablspi/audio/realtime/dialout/
      plugdev/video/render to mirror the stock runtime environment.
    - After/Wants now also includes swupdateprog-stub.service.
  * Added swupdateprog-stub: small UNIX-socket stub at
    /tmp/swupdateprog that satisfies MoveControlModeHandler's
    libswupdate `progress_ipc_connect()` retry-loop. Without this,
    MoveControlModeHandler spin-retries connect() forever and never
    opens /dev/ablspi0.0, leaving MoveLauncher stuck on the boot
    splash. The Debian `swupdate` package itself is compiled with
    -DCONFIG_SIGNED_IMAGES and refuses to start without a public key
    file — running the real daemon was simpler to bypass than to
    configure. Ships as /usr/local/sbin/swupdateprog-stub.py and an
    enabled systemd unit.
  * postinst: enable + start swupdateprog-stub.service.
  * BUILD.md: document the ConnMan/net.connman WiFi-status gap (stock
    uses ConnMan; we use NetworkManager; networking works fine but the
    on-device WiFi icon stays "disconnected" until we add an NM-state
    → ConnMan-D-Bus bridge or co-install ConnMan).

 -- Move Port <move-port@localhost>  Wed, 13 May 2026 19:20:00 +0000

move-bringup (1.0.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * /data is now a real mount point. Ships data.mount, a systemd .mount
    unit that bind-mounts /var/lib/move-data over /data. MoveLauncher
    gates a "No Data Partition" cosmetic display on
    `findmnt --mountpoint /data` succeeding; with the bind-mount in
    place the check passes and the message disappears. Avoids the SD
    partition surgery the disabled move-firstboot-data.service would
    have done — same outcome from MoveLauncher's perspective, no risk
    of bricking the install on first boot.
  * move-bringup.postinst now creates /var/lib/move-data and the
    expected subtree (CoreLibrary, log, Scratch, settings, UserData
    owned by ableton), enables + starts data.mount, and is safely
    idempotent.
  * move-launcher.service now Requires=data.mount so the launcher
    won't start until /data is mounted.

