move-bringup (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * move-bringup: switched to architecture arm64 to ship the new
    /usr/sbin/move-xmos-init binary alongside the existing config tree.
  * Added move-xmos-init: a one-shot replay of the stock MoveLauncher
    boot-time SysEx batch (Universal ID Request + cmd 0x42/0x25/0x3A/
    0x1E/0x47/0x0D/0x37 + CC 0/126), reverse-engineered from a
    movesniff capture of a stock Move boot. After this fires, the XMOS
    streams pad/knob/button events as plain MIDI on cable 0 so
    schwung-spi-based userspace (vimana2r, etc.) sees them. Stock
    MoveLauncher continues to work because it does the same handshake.
  * move-xmos-init.service: oneshot, runs after udev-settle and before
    move-launcher; gated by ConditionPathExists=/dev/ablspi0.0.
  * move-launcher.service: depends on move-xmos-init.service so the
    handshake completes before MoveLauncher's own attempt.

